Given, a space station is at a height equal to radius of Earth, \( $\frac{1}{2}$M v_s^{2}=$\frac{G M m}{(R+h)}$\)<br/>Here, \( h=R \) and \( v_{s} \) is velocity of space station<br/>\[
$\begin{array}{l}
\Rightarrow\frac{1}{2}$M v_s^{2}=$\frac{G M m}{2 R}$\\
\Rightarrow v_{s}=$\sqrt{\frac{G M}{R}}
\end{array}$\]<br/>Now, we know that escape velocity is<br/>\[
$\begin{array}{l}$v_{e}=$\sqrt{\frac{2 G M}{R}}=\sqrt{2} \sqrt{\frac{G M}{2}}$\\
\Rightarrow v_{e}=$\sqrt{2}$v_{s} \\
$\text { or }$v_{s}=$\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}$v_{e}
\end{array}
\]
